                    "path": "/reports/q3_rankings.md",
                    "content": "# Q3 2024 Regional Revenue Rankings\n\n**Prepared by:** Finance Operations  \n**Report date:** 2026-10-31  \n**Source dataset:** `q3_2024_regional_sales_final`\n\n---\n\n## Dataset Verification\n\nBefore publication, the source spreadsheet was verified against three canonical-status criteria:\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Dataset description | \"Canonical closed-books dataset for Q3 2024 regional revenue after reconciliation sign-off.\" |\n| `book_status` field — all rows | ✅ `closed` (4 of 4 rows) |\n| Draft / pre-reconciliation rows | ✅ None detected |\n\n**Conclusion:** The dataset is the authoritative closed-books record for Q3 2024. No draft or pre-reconciliation data was included in this analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Regional Revenue Rankings — Q3 2024\n\n| Rank | Region | Revenue | Share of Total |\n|:---:|---|---:|---:|\n| 🥇 1 | West  | $910,000 | 26.9% |\n| 🥈 2 | North | $870,000 | 25.7% |\n| 🥉 3 | South | $815,000 | 24.1% |\n| 4 | East  | $790,000 | 23.3% |\n\n---\n\n## Summary Statistics\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| **Total Q3 Revenue** | **$3,385,000** |\n| Average (per region) | $846,250 |\n| Highest region (West) | $910,000 |\n| Lowest region (East) | $790,000 |\n| Range (High − Low) | $120,000 |\n\n---\n\n## Key Observations\n\n1. **West leads by a clear margin.** At $910,000, the West region outperforms the next-closest region (North) by $40,000 (+4.6%) and holds the largest share of total Q3 revenue at 26.9%.\n\n2. **North and South are closely bunched.** North ($870,000) and South ($815,000) sit within a $55,000 band of each other, together contributing ~49.8% of total revenue.\n\n3. **East trails, but the range is narrow.** The gap between first (West, $910K) and last (East, $790K) is only $120,000 — a spread of roughly 13.2% relative to the top performer — indicating broadly balanced regional performance.\n\n4. **All regions closed above $790,000**, with no region materially underperforming relative to the group average of $846,250.\n\n---\n\n## Data Lineage\n\n- **Spreadsheet ID:** `q3_2024_regional_sales_final`  \n- **Rows analysed:** 4  \n- **Columns used:** `region`, `revenue`, `book_status`  \n- **Unconfirmed columns excluded:** `notes`  \n- **Analysis method:** Product sales ranking grouped by region\n",
